One contract so the four parallel tasks agree.

BACKEND (additive to kopi/models.py):
- InsightsRequest{doc_nos: list[str] 1..25, profile: Profile, query: str|None}
- EligibilitySummary{met, unmet, unknown: int; blocker: EligibilityCheck|None (first unmet); open_question: EligibilityCheck|None (first unknown)}
- MarketBand{similar_count: int; median_amount, p25_amount, p75_amount: float|None}
- TenderInsight{doc_no; eligibility: EligibilitySummary; snippet: str|None (<=240 chars, the description sentence closest to the query); items: int; two_envelope: bool|None; procurement_method: str|None; market: MarketBand|None}
- ChatRequest.bid: bool = False
- MemoryNote{id, text, source: 'kopi'|'you', created}
- BidStage = Literal['qualify','clarify','draft','review','submit']
- BidMemory{notes: list[MemoryNote]; stage: BidStage|None; next_step: str|None; updated: datetime|None}
- MemoryRequest{text 1..1000}
- SessionFile.kind: Literal['draft','upload'] = 'draft'

ROUTES (kopi/api/app.py), through the Store:
- POST /search/insights (Authed, Read) -> list[TenderInsight]
- GET /sessions/{id}/memory (AppOnly) -> BidMemory
- POST /sessions/{id}/memory (AppOnly) {text} -> BidMemory (adds a 'you' note)
- POST /sessions/{id}/memory/{note_id}/forget (AppOnly) -> BidMemory
- POST /sessions/{id}/uploads?name= (AppOnly; raw body <=8 MB; .pdf .md .txt .csv only) -> SessionFile(kind='upload')
- GET /sessions/{id}/files lists drafts and uploads; GET .../files/{name} serves uploads with their media type.

Store delegation:
- Store.insights -> kopi.insights.insights(store, doc_nos, profile, query), a module whose body KP-32 writes;
- memory and uploads -> Copilot methods in kopi/sandbox.py, whose bodies KP-33 writes.

WEB: api-types.ts regenerated; KopiApi gains insights(), memory(), remember(), forget(), upload(); LiveApi and MockApi implement them (the mock insights come from the fixtures and the mock's eligibility and market rules, and mock memory and uploads are in-memory). lib/bids.ts: a Bid record in localStorage (doc_no, title, agency, closing, url, session_id|null, started), useBids(), startBid(notice) -> '/bid/?doc=…&start=1'. Tracked submissions carry over as bids.

web/components/search/*.

Each card:
- agency initials disc and agency · category;
- title (displayTitle, highlights);
- a 'why it matched' snippet with the query words marked;
- chips: eligibility (green 'Eligible · N met' / red 'Blocker: <requirement>' / grey 'N unknown'), closing (red <=3 days), method, two envelopes, and value band 'S$149k–705k past awards';
- a match meter with the exact score in a tooltip;
- hover and focus actions: Start bid (primary pill, lib/bids startBid), Ask Kopi, Open.

Insights are fetched in batches of 25 after the hits render, with skeleton chips meanwhile.

At >=1280px a right-hand preview pane (sticky in #kopi-panel) shows the selected tender: key facts, the eligibility list, items, and description excerpt, with the same actions.

Keyboard: j/k (arrow keys) move, Enter opens, b starts a bid.

At 390 the cards stack cleanly, with no preview pane. D26 style throughout.

